@startuml code-generation-organize-imports-sequence
title Optimize Imports (D4 §3.4) — the one new protocol flow this phase adds

actor User
participant "ide-ui\n(app.rs)" as UI
participant "LspBridge" as Bridge
participant "ide-lsp\nconnection task" as Lsp
participant "Language server\n(rust-analyzer / gopls / ...)" as Server

User -> UI: press ⌘⌥O / Ctrl+Alt+O
UI -> Bridge: request_organize_imports(path)
Bridge -> Lsp: LspRequest::OrganizeImports { path }
note right of Lsp
  Own pending-id slot, independent of
  pending_code_action_id / pending_resolve_id.
  Whole-document range, not the caret position
  lsp.code_actions was built from.
end note
Lsp -> Server: textDocument/codeAction\ncontext.only: ["source.organizeImports"]

alt server returns an entry with a usable edit
  Server --> Lsp: CodeAction[] (one entry)
  opt entry needs resolving
    Lsp -> Server: codeAction/resolve
    Server --> Lsp: resolved CodeAction
  end
  Lsp --> Bridge: LspEvent::WorkspaceEditReady { edit: Some(..), label: Some("Optimize Imports") }
  Bridge --> UI: (existing) handle_workspace_edit_ready
  UI -> User: edit applied immediately, no preview
else server returns empty (guaranteed for rust-analyzer, §1)
  Server --> Lsp: CodeAction[] (empty)
  Lsp --> Bridge: LspEvent::WorkspaceEditReady { edit: None, label: None }
  Bridge --> UI: (existing) handle_workspace_edit_ready
  UI -> User: "Optimize Imports: nothing to apply"
end

@enduml
